# Panel 260's R2 (provisional, author ratification pending): a header of the
# program's own named `hero_util.h` is none of the platform layer's files,
# which are the runtime's own list by path, so a group over it saying `layer`
# binds nothing of the layer and is refused at the word, the fix taking it out
# (the critic's `ownnamed`, declared).
extern "hero_util.h" layer  #~ ffi_layer_unreached
    function util_answer() -> i64

function main()
    print(util_answer())
